<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Prague</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Prague is the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czech-republic">Czech Republic</a> and historically of the Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bohemia">Bohemia</a>. In the late nineteenth century it was one of the most economically dynamic cities of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a>, along with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/budapest">Budapest</a>. It was also a centre of Czech national life within the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> monarchy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/prague.jpg" alt="Prague" width="320" height="190" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Moyan Brenn from Italy · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Prague_(6365119737).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
